########################################################################

DOCUMENT();      

loadMacros(
   "PGstandard.pl",     # Standard macros for PG language
   "MathObjects.pl",
   #"source.pl",        # allows code to be displayed on certain sites.
   #"PGcourse.pl",      # Customization file for the course
);

# Print problem number and point value (weight) for the problem
TEXT(beginproblem());

# Show which answers are correct and which ones are incorrect
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 1;

##############################################################
#
#  Setup
#
#
Context("Numeric");

$q1 = Compute("-1"); #K8 Q8.1
$q2 = Compute("-1"); #K8 Q8.2
$q3 = Compute("-log(25/7)"); #K8 Q8.3
$q4 = Compute("-log(25/7)"); #K8 Q8.4
$q5 = Compute("-0.297"); #K8 Q8.5
$q6 = Compute("-0.297"); #K8 Q8.6





##############################################################
#
#  Text
#
#

Context()->texStrings;
BEGIN_TEXT
Here is some additional computational practice with circulation and flux in \( \mathbb{R}^2. \) Consider a fluid flow in \( \mathbb{R}^2 \) defined by the vector field \(	F(x,y) = \big(\dfrac{y}{x^2+y^2+1}, \dfrac{x}{x^2+y^2+1} \big) \).
$BR
\{ image( "k1-curl-div.png", width=>300, height=>300 ) \} $BR

Let \( R \) be the solid rectangle with vertices \( (0,0), (0,2), (3,0) \) and \( (3,2). \) Let \( C = \partial R \) be the counterclockwise oriented boundary of the rectangle. Use WolframAlpha to numerically evaluate any  explicit integrals. Round decimals to two decimal places. $BR $BR

1. Determine if the point \( (2,2) \) is a source or a sink. Type 1 for source and -1 for sink. $BR
\{$q1->ans_rule\} $BR

2. Determine if the fluid is swirling clockwise or counterclockwise near \( (-3,1). \) Type -1 for clockwise and 1 for counterclockwise. $BR
\{$q2->ans_rule\} $BR

3. Compute the circulation of the fluid along \( C \) by direct calculation. $BR
\{$q3->ans_rule\} $BR

4. Evaluate \( \iint_R \text{curl}(F) dA \) by direct calculation.  $BR
\{$q4->ans_rule\} $BR

5. Compute the net flux across \( C \) by direct calculation. $BR
\{$q5->ans_rule\} $BR

6. Evaluate \( \iint_R \text{div}(F) dA \) by direct calculation. $BR
\{$q6->ans_rule\} $BR



END_TEXT
Context()->normalStrings;

##############################################################
#
#  Answers
#
#

ANS($q1->with(tolerance=>.01)->cmp);
ANS($q2->with(tolerance=>.01)->cmp);
ANS($q3->with(tolerance=>.02)->cmp);
ANS($q4->with(tolerance=>.02)->cmp);
ANS($q5->with(tolerance=>.02)->cmp);
ANS($q6->with(tolerance=>.02)->cmp);


# default tolerance is .01 or one percent.


ENDDOCUMENT();        